Z||000008||1FST2M6||01-10-2001||01:32 PM||||save your money... tape a white china marker to the strut tower-tip up. touching the deck lid. drive the hell out of the car. you'll see there is MAYBE 1/8" of deflection. (i'm sure most of that was the duck tape not able to handle the shaking and g's) the back of the car (trunk area) is connecting the two towers(with a 3"x1.5/8" tube). the cockpit of the car is only 10" from them ALSO welded to the towers.. the cradel is attached (better with aluminum bushings or an 88) i'd say save your $ and get sway bars. there is a much better mechanical advantage there and a more pronounced taming of the chassis<P>just my $.02 <P><BR>ok just read the rest of the thread... for show..  ok get it.. but bright Red or Blue sway bars are pretty obvious too and functional... <BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
