Z||000018||1FST2M6||01-11-2001||09:05 AM||||LMAO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> GT Bastard! <P>anywho... for show points yeah it's one more shiney thing you can ad for glitz. and the bedazzelment of the judges.. thats really all they look at.. not use-ability or installation quality(local judges anyway).. I've been on the local show scene for 3-4 years and watched the judges and you can have a KILLER ride that just with a simple glance you can tell that the owner USES the car to is ability (Solo racing or Drag) like(running Konis and tuned springs etc.)but right next to it you'll have a gimp-o-roidal sped with shiney parts (stock struts and Coil overs turned all the way down) and he'll get the trophy over the more useful vehicle. (sorry to bring imports into this)(never showed my 86.. have shown my GT... in "construction" class)<P>My 86 SE pulled 1.13g on the skid pad without a strut bar but with a rear sway and stock front bar. (driven by an SCCA Pro IT driver at Road Atl.) without the bar it was faster in the 1/4 but nearly a full second slower and less stable on a road course.   <P>ok... anyone near a Solo course or other closed road course? that has access to both bars, and decent timing equipment? test with one and take it off and install the other..  and install both and then let us know. obviously we'll have to wait till the the season starts back up though for real track #s. not booty-o-meter #s.  a G-tech accelerometer would be close but you can make it read false by jerking the wheel.. my car pulled 1.9gs once with a g-tech.. I KNOW thats not right. i'm not a smooth driver so i'll stick to daily driving and 1/8th & 1/4mi. runs. it's too bad noone makes a real lateral acceleration dyno thats consistant and repeatable. just the simple mechanics of the sway bar vs the strut bar should show you which is the more dramatic of improvement. <P>why am i the man? I'm just along for the ride...  ||||reg||1
